# Coordinates of the third binary extension

The 384 rows are obtained by breadth-first enumeration of the two published
permutations. The four quotient blocks have labels `(x / 2) % 4`. Kernel
coordinates use the four basis permutations recorded by `kernelRows`.
The companion module checks the words, transitions and extension identities
in Lean's kernel. These data assert no unverified enumeration result.

Source context: Huppert--Blackburn, *Finite Groups III*, XII.1.18(b), p.314.
The coordinates are independently computed, not tables printed in the book.
Regeneration: `source/generate.py` in this directory.
-/

